WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.729
Command and control means unauthorized communication that allows an affected asset, account,

00:00:04.729 --> 00:00:09.744
workload, or service to receive direction or send status outside normal trust boundaries.

00:00:09.744 --> 00:00:13.987
Defenders should treat this stage as a question about communication evidence,

00:00:13.987 --> 00:00:17.073
not as a lesson in setup or evasion.

00:00:17.073 --> 00:00:22.088
Useful signals may appear in DNS logs, proxy logs, firewall records, endpoint telemetry,

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:25.945
cloud network flow records, identity events, or SaaS activity logs.

00:00:25.945 --> 00:00:27.874
The details vary by environment.

00:00:27.874 --> 00:00:30.960
A workstation, a container workload, a cloud function,

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.818
and a compromised account may all create different communication patterns.

00:00:34.818 --> 00:00:37.904
Defensive controls include egress filtering, destination allowlists, segmentation,

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.990
proxy inspection, anomaly detection, and rapid containment paths.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:44.847
Analysts should ask what communicated, where it communicated, how often,

00:00:44.847 --> 00:00:49.476
through which control point, and whether that behavior matches expected business activity.

00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:51.791
Containment decisions should be evidence based.

00:00:51.791 --> 00:00:55.263
Isolating a host, disabling a credential, blocking a destination,

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:57.963
or segmenting a workload can reduce risk,

00:00:57.963 --> 00:01:01.049
but those actions should be recorded and coordinated.

00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:05.678
The value of this stage is to make outbound visibility and containment

00:01:05.678 --> 00:01:07.993
planning part of normal defensive readiness.

00:01:07.993 --> 00:01:13.393
This stage is a reminder that outbound visibility matters as much as inbound defense.

00:01:13.393 --> 00:01:17.636
If the organization cannot explain which systems can reach which destinations,

00:01:17.636 --> 00:01:19.951
containment becomes slower and less precise.

00:01:19.951 --> 00:01:24.580
Well-governed egress makes unusual communication easier to notice and easier to limit.
